WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.294
A few days ago,
a racially insensitive email surfaced

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:05.463
from UBA board president, Cybil Reynolds.

00:00:06.381 --> 00:00:11.886
The email contained comments about me.
I haven't spoken out in public until now.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:15.557
And here to join me as I do so is
the woman who wrote those comments.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.476
UBA board president, Cybil Reynolds,
thank you for being here.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:19.769
Thank you for having me on.

00:00:20.395 --> 00:00:24.315
Now I know there was some furor,
well deserved,

00:00:24.399 --> 00:00:27.944
over the statement that UBA
issued some days ago.

00:00:28.737 --> 00:00:32.574
It was inadequate, to say the very least.

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:38.079
The mistake was mine and mine alone,
and I'm here to apologize in person.

00:00:39.247 --> 00:00:43.668
Chris, I'm--
I am deeply sorry for what I said.

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:47.005
Even in the heat of
a contentious hiring decision,

00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:50.341
nothing can excuse what I said.

00:00:50.967 --> 00:00:52.844
You mean calling me Aunt Jemima?

00:00:53.428 --> 00:00:55.805
I didn't exactly call you Aunt--

00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:57.891
I wanna set the record straight.

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:03.396
You know that Aunt Jemima was on boxes
of pancake mix and not cereal, right?

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.939
I guess I know that now.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:10.195
But this is about more than
just an offhand comment.

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:13.948
The irony of your joke is that
the Pearl Milling Company

00:01:14.032 --> 00:01:17.952
used the image and likeness of
a Black woman to sell a brand,

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.371
I'm sure, with no profit participation.

00:01:20.455 --> 00:01:24.334
My question is what brand
am I helping UBA to sell, in your eyes?

00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:29.297
Look, words matter. Actions matter more.

00:01:29.297 --> 00:01:33.802
And UBA has been sorely inactive
when it comes to equity and inclusion.

00:01:34.385 --> 00:01:38.139
Now, the board isn't involved
with day-to-day operations.

00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:41.559
We leave that to
the capable leadership of our CEO.

00:01:42.894 --> 00:01:49.025
But when that leadership falters,
I have a duty to step in.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.611
Don't you f*cking dare.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:55.490
-She firing shots at Cory?
-He deserves them.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.742
I'm not sure you're answering my question.

00:01:57.826 --> 00:02:00.537
-Oh.
-But let's talk about stepping in.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.871
What would that look like?

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:05.166
Do you even think it's possible
to win back the trust of UBA's employees?

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:08.586
You know something? I do.

00:02:09.754 --> 00:02:10.964
I do think it's possible.

00:02:11.047 --> 00:02:15.760
And it'll start with a dialogue
between UBA employees and the board.

00:02:15.844 --> 00:02:21.724
From now on, you all will have
a voice at every single board meeting.

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:23.726
Now is the time for transparency.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.228
That's great to hear, truly.

00:02:26.396 --> 00:02:29.107
In the interest of transparency,

00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:34.821
Was I hired for a permanent
anchor position because I am Black?

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.950
Obviously not. No.

00:02:39.033 --> 00:02:40.660
But you see my confusion, right?

00:02:40.743 --> 00:02:44.998
Because you used a clumsy racist comment

00:02:45.081 --> 00:02:47.125
to complain about my hiring.

00:02:47.208 --> 00:02:49.836
Did you think I wasn't qualified,
was that it?

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:54.174
Well, now in point of fact, at that time,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.634
I did not believe you were qualified.

00:02:56.634 --> 00:03:00.013
Let me rephrase. You were untested.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.973
Well, that's not exactly true.

00:03:01.973 --> 00:03:03.975
Were you aware that I was cue tested

00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:09.063
more than any other person who
has ever anchored this show?

00:03:09.647 --> 00:03:11.983
That I had to have eight different
approval meetings

00:03:12.066 --> 00:03:15.195
in addition to the strategy discussions
about my hair?

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:16.654
I was unaware.

00:03:16.654 --> 00:03:21.993
And I still found time to
spend weekends with four former anchors,

00:03:22.076 --> 00:03:24.370
developing my on-air skills.

00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:27.373
Well, now that-that is impressive.
That's very admirable.

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:29.834
That aside,
I don't understand why you used

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:32.128
a racialized image when discussing me.

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.839
Is that how you see me?

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:39.010
Is that how you see us?

00:03:50.313 --> 00:03:55.818
Would you want your entire career
reduced to one unthinking,

00:03:55.818 --> 00:03:57.987
bone-headed thing you said in an email?

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:02.408
Haven't you ever said anything
that later you came to regret

00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:04.077
when speaking casually?

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:06.955
You're in a leadership position
at this network.

00:04:06.955 --> 00:04:08.289
And on your watch,

00:04:08.957 --> 00:04:13.962
you let employees of color
be systematically devalued.

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.881
Is that something to be casual about?

00:04:17.548 --> 00:04:19.300
Donny,
tell the camera to push in on Cybil,

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.928
-and keep pushing until I see her pores.
-We're supposed to break.

00:04:22.011 --> 00:04:23.972
-You want me to cut--
-No. No.

00:04:24.055 --> 00:04:27.058
Okay. Camera two, push in. Closer.

00:04:27.141 --> 00:04:28.142
No.

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:32.272
I was careless,
and there isn't any excuse.

00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:35.191
But you have to understand.

00:04:35.191 --> 00:04:38.444
We don't just give this opportunity
to anyone.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:43.491
Anyone who sits in that chair
has to be grateful--

00:04:43.574 --> 00:04:44.575
I sh--

00:04:45.535 --> 00:04:46.577
There it is.

00:04:47.578 --> 00:04:48.579
I should be grateful?

00:04:48.579 --> 00:04:52.041
Well,
that your job is so very hard to get.

00:04:56.379 --> 00:05:00.425
I want to say,
as for UBA as an institution,

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:02.427
going forward, I think we've--

00:05:02.427 --> 00:05:07.348
We should move on from this climate
where racial divisions are exploited.

00:05:07.807 --> 00:05:09.892
But that's every climate though,
wouldn't you say?

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:15.898
Sh*t.

00:05:18.359 --> 00:05:22.780
But yes,
we will move on from institutional racism

00:05:23.031 --> 00:05:24.240
right after this break.

